  "scoreProvenance": [
    "EXT: All four unchanged sounding Liu piano voices are extracted separately; these are notation identities, not recovered recorded hands. MEAS: 497 canonical voice events / 404 distinct pitch-onset pairs versus legacy 402/402 comprise 93 coincident voice-unisons and two genuinely missing A2 quarter attacks at q7.5/q23.5 (bars 4/12; bassvoices a4, source lines 208/216) beneath bassvoicestwo A2 ties starting q6/q22 (lines 245–246/254–255). Both independent attacks and held voices are retained.",
    "MEAS: Two A1 grace onsets relocate from q8.3697917/q24.3697917 to q8.3854167/q24.3854167 under modern LilyPond; they are not new main notes. Eleven shared-note duration differences are written-staccato playback policy, and two are grace-adjacent tie gates. Those A2 ties have written spans of 2.5Q; rendered MIDI gates are 2.3854167Q because the following grace steals time. These realizations do not establish measured recording key releases. No source pitch, repeat or written rest is removed; recording edition remains provisional.",
    "Read content/listen/schumann-kinderszenen-happiness.mjs and cache/analysis/schumann-kinderszenen-happiness.txt. Harmonic trajectories suggest A0–28, B28–46, A46–68, B68–90; these are coarse, not forced alignment anchors.",
    "Opened Henle critical notes p299, https://www.henle.de/media/05/bf/e6/1690899698/9924-1690899698-sync.pdf: FE2 writes repeats out; the D.C. at16 may be a manuscript remnant. This documents edition/order ambiguity, not proof of Betts's choice. The proposed return is subject to pitch/order inspection.",
    "DCML reference harmony https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DCMLab/schumann_kinderszenen/main/harmonies/n05.harmonies.tsv confirms the borrowed F-major region (local bIII of D); no reference-corpus notes or harmony labels are copied into this Mutopia-derived score."
  ],
